\f4\fs26 \'93It took me ages to reconstruct the genetic lines but I can unequivocally say the sample dates back from the first half of the 20th century. You are carrying the clone of a long deceased man named Richard Dawkins, but there appears to be a few added sequences.\'94 \
\'93The Dawkins!\'94 Cracker hit the floor laughing and did not stop until his stomach muscles threatened to tear and his face ached. \'93The fuckin\'92 Dawkins!\'94\
\'93I am looking at the helix and it is perfect, I mean absolutely zero copying errors \'96 there are usually a one or two, but in this case the sequence is flawless. I will have to isolate and analyse the added sequences. That will take some considerable time.\'94 Her eyes remained glued to the holograms as they hung in the air. The Hybrid T-Virus was already working on the growing embryo, correcting any errors and maximising development in-utero, seamlessly blending artificial DNA with the base genetic material of the clone. \
Dr Logan, on the other hand had just been hit with a wave of MDMA and was running between the two hugging them and sincerely saying, \'93I love you.\'94 \
\'93Richard Dawkins? What did those creeps do to me?\'94 Sarah was replaying the events on the travelator, but could not immediately pin down anything in particular. She did not know whether to laugh or cry, but did neither. She had not thought she would ever find herself in such a predicament and had no contingency plan whatsoever. \'93How can it be done without me noticing?\'94\
\'93It does seem unlikely, but I suppose it is a possibility. There are black market cloning devices, but they don\'92t usually get such quality results. They keep the clone in stasis until implantation, without refrigeration. It implants the duplicate into the uterus directly through the abdominal wall. Anyone can manage it, once it is placed on the stomach, it automatically penetrates and implants. All in the matter of half a second.\'94 Kathy took Sarah\'92s hand and held it lightly. \'93Sarah, you have been violated, far worse than any mere assault. You should contact the police.\'94\
\'93Thank you, Kathy. I appreciate your kindness. I will seek my own justice on this one, thank you.\'94 Sarah did not know how she could possibly face her new colleagues if this was to get out. She began planning a visit to old Kleo and the gang on the travelator very soon. \
\'93I don\'92t know what to say.\'94 The gravity of the situation had suddenly hit Cracker. Now that he knew she was pregnant, an entirely new Sarah stood before him and he found his symmetry completely askew. In his immature youth he would have insisted the parasitic tumour-with-legs be treated with immediate removal. Only after the malignancy was excised could he look upon the woman as anything other than a diseased patient seeking a cure. Now, however, with Sarah standing before him, he saw a vulnerable, frightened girl in profound crisis. He wanted to take her in his arms, hold her close, assure her that everything will be alright and then sit her in a comfy chair with a nice cup of tea. He was muddled and kind of grossed out by these warm and fuzzy feelings. \'93What are you going to do?\'94\
\'93I don\'92t know. I will have to think about it.\'94 Sarah started walking toward to front security doors to disappear into the night. \'93Don\'92t follow me.\'94 Her voice fading as she trudged away.\
\'93That did not go well, did it Cracker?\'94 Kathy cuddled up and he hugged her back. \'93You like her, huh?\'94\
\'93She must not come to any harm.\'94 \
\'93Always the protector.\'94 She hugged him harder. \'93Want to go patching?\'94\
\'93Yep.\'94
